		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: DM-1701 charger on 12V ?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4936&amp;p=36684#p36684"><![CDATA[
In the charger base VT1701 there is a SC6038 charging controller, datasheet <span style="text-decoration:line-through">see attached</span> is not allowed to attach.<br><br><a href="https://u.dianyuan.com/upload/space/2011/03/26/1301101488-424710.pdf" class="postlink">https://u.dianyuan.com/upload/space/201 ... 424710.pdf</a><br><br>Its Vin(max) is rated for 18V, so it might safely work at a 12V power supply, but I wouldn't recommend to use it without additional protection at a car lighter plug.<br><br>73 de Bert<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3024">DD5XL</a> — Thu Apr 10, 2025 9:42 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
