		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4936&amp;p=36070#p36070"><![CDATA[
My 10V 1A PSU for the charger broke yesterday in the Europlug pin, as the radio was delivered with a US charger I had replaced it with one I bought on the European market. <br>Sometimes you wish you had UK plugs instead <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile">  <br><br>10V is a bit unusual, most of the other radios (RT3S/MD2017) use a 12V PSU for the charger base.<br><br>Anyone tried to run the base on 12V instead ?<br><br>The chip is marked HC5812 MSLX236 and I haven't found any datasheet on google for it.<br><br>Or I could replace the circuit with some other Li-ion charger circuit, maybe a USB-C based from Aliexpress ?<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2869&amp;sid=3dda80462fd11f905a5f63b47e80a300" class="postimage" alt="20250304_204210.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Wed Mar 05, 2025 7:20 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
